NAME
    menu-ext - select one value from an interactive terminal menu

SYNOPSIS
    menu-ext [-H <header>] [-F <footer>] [-B <bottom-footer>] -- <item> ...

DESCRIPTION
    menu-ext renders an interactive menu on /dev/tty while reserving standard
    output for the selected value.

    Each item is either:
        <text>
        <value>@:=<text>

    The first form displays and returns the same text. The second displays text
    but returns value.

    Up/Down or k/j move by one item, PageUp/PageDown move by a page, Enter
    selects, and q or Escape cancels.

OPTIONS
    -H <header>         Header at the top of the terminal.
    -F <footer>         Footer after the last visible item.
    -B <bottom-footer>  Footer anchored at the bottom.
    -h                  Write command usage.

EXIT STATUS
    0   A selection was made.
    1   The menu was cancelled.
    2   Invalid invocation or terminal/setup failure.
